A vehicle travels at constant speed around a wide circular track. It continuously sounds its horn, which emits a single note of frequency $1.2\text{ kHz}$. An observer is a large distance away from the track, as shown in the view from above in Fig. 4.1.
{{figure:figure_4_1}}
Fig. 4.1 (not to scale)
Fig. 4.2 shows the variation with time of the frequency $f$ of the sound of the horn that is detected by the observer. The time taken for the vehicle to travel once around the track is $T$.
{{figure:figure_4_2}}
Fig. 4.2

